<h2 class="mt-14">Consent and purchaser suppression for Product care</h2>
<p>Before launching product care automation, prove every app in the stack logs email and SMS consent auditably, with purchase events cutting promotional follow-up the moment checkout completes. In product care, mistimed sends after purchases, refunds, or support cases destroy channel value quicker than any creative miss.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented consent</td><td>Suppress product care marketing entirely until consent is documented</td><td>Without product care consent proof, marketing has no legal footing</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>Open product care with guidance and proof, not discounts</td><td>First-touch product care codes create discount dependence</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Product Care reminder with product context; discount withheld</td><td>Protects product care profit when purchase intent is hottest</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Suppress product care selling after checkout; educate instead</td><td>Spares product care buyers remorse and unsubscribes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>Freeze product care promos until refund or return closes</td><td>Open product care cases reset what the shopper tolerates</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Product Care sunset policy precedes complaint spikes</td><td>Product Care deliverability depends on pruning</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Product Care texting respects time and frequency rules</td><td>Text grievances hit product care programs hardest</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Product Care B2B routing stays account-specific</td><td>Product Care retail promos can violate B2B terms</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Product Care automation skips unverified domains first</td><td>Product Care list quality decides placement</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Product Care internal accounts never enter production</td><td>QA product care sends distort real performance</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>Product Care exceptions stay undocumented-free</td><td>Product Care consistency beats clever carve-outs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Legacy product care contacts re-opt before journeys</td><td>Old product care permission without records is a risk</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="mt-12">Margin, app costs, and pricing for Product care</h2>
<p>Product Care profit needs the whole ledger: subscription plus overages, SMS credits, capture and template spend, agency retainers, and product care discount margin against attributed revenue. Product Care rule: near fifteen percent stack-to-margin, cut product care complexity before chasing gains.</p>
<p>Pricing changes frequently and varies by region, contact volume, and contract term, so check the official pricing pages of every shortlisted app and model an eighteen-month total that includes a peak season. Free tiers ration contacts, sends, branching, or support — confirm which ceiling binds your product care plan first.</p>
