<h2 class="mt-12">Governance and documentation for product care</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Practice</th><th>Standard</th><th>Risk it prevents</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Flow ownership</td><td>product care ownership assigned journey by journey</td><td>Abandoned product care journeys mailing on</td></tr>
<tr><td>Naming convention</td><td>Name product care flows job-first, audience-second</td><td>Peak product care triage blind without naming</td></tr>
<tr><td>Change log</td><td>product care edits stamped, dated, explained</td><td>Unlogged product care changes hiding causes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Access control</td><td>Product Care seats on least privilege</td><td>product care rogue sends from open permissions</td></tr>
<tr><td>Quarterly flow review</td><td>Prune idle product care branches quarterly</td><td>Product Care bloat taxing each edit</td></tr>
<tr><td>Incident runbook</td><td>Product Care pause-and-notify runbook</td><td>Product Care harm airing too long</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="mt-12">Peak season readiness for product care</h2>
<ol>
<li>Lock product care flow edits a full fortnight before peak.</li>
<li>Prove product care flows on genuine transactions pre-peak.</li>
<li>For product care, confirm buyer and return exclusions hold.</li>
<li>For product care, grow control samples ahead of volume.</li>
<li>For product care, pre-commit text timing and frequency limits.</li>
<li>Price product care peaks against plan ceilings early.</li>
<li>Product Care placement watched every peak day.</li>
<li>Product Care undo paths recorded pre-campaign.</li>
</ol>
<p>For product care, schedule quarter-one review before the first send. Writing product care suppression rules, discount caps, and escalation paths down in week one saves weeks of peak-season triage and hands newcomers a working product care playbook.</p>
<p>Close each product care quarter with a written ledger — product care sends shipped, suppressions honored, margin retained, failed bets — so product care vendor decisions rest on one shared evidence file, not scattered memory.</p>
